<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Kondo & Asai (1995) Pomacanthus reaction-diffusion stripe insertion & Y-branch unzipping (Pomacanthus semicirculatus & Pomacanthus imperator (marine angelfish))",
        "Kondo & Asai (1995) Pomacanthus reaction-diffusion stripe insertion & Y-branch unzipping faithfully reproduces Pomacanthus semicirculatus & Pomacanthus imperator (marine angelfish) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Pomacanthus semicirculatus & Pomacanthus imperator (marine angelfish) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 93.1/100, audit 2026-10-19-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py> ;
    schema:about "Pomacanthus semicirculatus & Pomacanthus imperator (marine angelfish)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: 2D agent-field coupling on the curved domain, pigment-cell migration or Delta-Notch-type contact signalling, a conformal map of the real body outline, or 3D body-fin boundary mechanics",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 1D and 2D IMEX spectral solvers for the Kondo-Asai piecewise-linear saturating PDE across stationary domain doubling scales s in {1, 2, 4, 8} (body length 2, 4, 8, 16 cm -> 3, 6, 12, 24 stripes), subcritical inhibitor-diffusion control D_I = 0.050 < d_c D_A (0 stripes), continuous growing-domain kymograph (3 -> 6 -> 12 stripes), and 2D Y-branch horizontal unzipping (3 -> 4 stripes, +0.663 domain fraction displacement)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Computer-vision segmentation of juvenile Pomacanthus semicirculatus specimen (`pomacanthus_semicirculatus_specimen.jpg`, CC BY-SA 4.0): 115 row-wise inter-stripe spacings (3.80 mm at 40 mm body span, CV = 0.34), primary/secondary prominence ratio 2.65x, bimodal Kondo-Asai waveform r = 0.858, and (Pass 3) structure-tensor concentric-arc fit (centre (262, 217) px, 8 arc radii, curvature-corrected radial spacing 2.62 mm, CV 0.28)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 3: curvilinear C-shaped polar-sector solver (rho in [0.25, 1], theta in [-100, 100] deg, 48 x 96, sparse-LU IMEX) with growing outer radius; 3 -> 6 concentric arcs at s* = 2.18 with mid-trough inhibitor trace I_mid(s) against the zero-activator threshold c_3/|c_2| = 0.625; 1D hybrid field + 128-cell iridophore/melanophore agent lattice with contact rules and bounded feedback kappa on c_3/c_5, ablated over kappa in {0, 0.005, 0.01, 0.02}",
        "reported_in_source: Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) Kybernetik 12:30-39 short-range autocatalytic activation and long-range lateral inhibition",
        "reported_in_source: Kondo & Asai (1995) Nature 376(6543):765-768 piecewise-linear saturating Gierer-Meinhardt reaction-diffusion PDE on an expanding skin domain L(t) = L_0 exp(gamma t), mid-trough secondary stripe insertion cascade (3 -> 6 -> 12 -> 24 stripes) in Pomacanthus semicirculatus, and 2D horizontal Y-junction branch point unzipping in Pomacanthus imperator",
        "reported_in_source: Nakamasu et al. (2009) PNAS 106:8429-8434 pigment-cell interaction network (short-range mutual exclusion, long-range support) and Bullara & De Decker (2015) lattice chromatophore model",
        "transfer_boundary: The agent layer is 1D on a periodic L = 6 lambda_c domain, so the wavelength is quantised to L/6 and only stripe contrast responds to the feedback; the rule probabilities (0.9 / 0.1 / update rate 0.35 / softness 0.3) are modelling choices, not values from Nakamasu et al. (2009)",
        "transfer_boundary: The curvilinear domain is an idealised polar sector (fixed rho_in = 0.25, theta_half = 100 deg), not the specimen's body silhouette; its centre and radial extent are not fitted to the specimen's concentric centre, so arc angular spans are not compared",
        "transfer_boundary: The mid-trough threshold c_3/|c_2| = 0.625 is the A = 0 sufficient condition; the simulated insertion fires at I_mid = 0.742 because flanking arcs supply activator diffusively" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Pisces (Ichthyes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Pomacanthus" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py; output: docs/media/pomacanthus_stripe_insertion_comparison.png; organism: Pomacanthus semicirculatus & Pomacanthus imperator (marine angelfish); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 9fca66f1ec5b7b985311e657c901c9004c5c9be93f2d029fa8365f8bf5322678; artifact_sha256: 92f926e73a7ebb81a69b893404cb09fadddfe38cba44064f55014e57a01e18c0; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/pomacanthus_stripe_insertion/pomacanthus_semicirculatus_specimen.jpg=5564f850c1905fb6..., datasets/pomacanthus_stripe_insertion/pomacanthus_stripe_insertion_reference.json=915a886aac71c336..., datasets/pomacanthus_stripe_insertion/scout_manifest.json=bf877731da64b97b...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Kondo & Asai (1995) Nature 376(6543):765-768 piecewise-linear saturating Gierer-Meinhardt reaction-diffusion PDE on an expanding skin domain L(t) = L_0 exp(gamma t), mid-trough secondary stripe insertion cascade (3 -> 6 -> 12 -> 24 stripes) in Pomacanthus semicirculatus, and 2D horizontal Y-junction branch point unzipping in Pomacanthus imperator | Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) Kybernetik 12:30-39 short-range autocatalytic activation and long-range lateral inhibition | Nakamasu et al. (2009) PNAS 106:8429-8434 pigment-cell interaction network (short-range mutual exclusion, long-range support) and Bullara & De Decker (2015) lattice chromatophore model; reconstructed_in_script: 1D and 2D IMEX spectral solvers for the Kondo-Asai piecewise-linear saturating PDE across stationary domain doubling scales s in {1, 2, 4, 8} (body length 2, 4, 8, 16 cm -> 3, 6, 12, 24 stripes), subcritical inhibitor-diffusion control D_I = 0.050 < d_c D_A (0 stripes), continuous growing-domain kymograph (3 -> 6 -> 12 stripes), and 2D Y-branch horizontal unzipping (3 -> 4 stripes, +0.663 domain fraction displacement) | Pass 3: curvilinear C-shaped polar-sector solver (rho in [0.25, 1], theta in [-100, 100] deg, 48 x 96, sparse-LU IMEX) with growing outer radius; 3 -> 6 concentric arcs at s* = 2.18 with mid-trough inhibitor trace I_mid(s) against the zero-activator threshold c_3/|c_2| = 0.625; 1D hybrid field + 128-cell iridophore/melanophore agent lattice with contact rules and bounded feedback kappa on c_3/c_5, ablated over kappa in {0, 0.005, 0.01, 0.02} | Computer-vision segmentation of juvenile Pomacanthus semicirculatus specimen (`pomacanthus_semicirculatus_specimen.jpg`, CC BY-SA 4.0): 115 row-wise inter-stripe spacings (3.80 mm at 40 mm body span, CV = 0.34), primary/secondary prominence ratio 2.65x, bimodal Kondo-Asai waveform r = 0.858, and (Pass 3) structure-tensor concentric-arc fit (centre (262, 217) px, 8 arc radii, curvature-corrected radial spacing 2.62 mm, CV 0.28); transfer_boundary: The curvilinear domain is an idealised polar sector (fixed rho_in = 0.25, theta_half = 100 deg), not the specimen's body silhouette; its centre and radial extent are not fitted to the specimen's concentric centre, so arc angular spans are not compared | The agent layer is 1D on a periodic L = 6 lambda_c domain, so the wavelength is quantised to L/6 and only stripe contrast responds to the feedback; the rule probabilities (0.9 / 0.1 / update rate 0.35 / softness 0.3) are modelling choices, not values from Nakamasu et al. (2009) | The mid-trough threshold c_3/|c_2| = 0.625 is the A = 0 sufficient condition; the simulated insertion fires at I_mid = 0.742 because flanking arcs supply activator diffusively; does_not_claim: 2D agent-field coupling on the curved domain, pigment-cell migration or Delta-Notch-type contact signalling, a conformal map of the real body outline, or 3D body-fin boundary mechanics]" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/376765a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms7971>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0808622106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1387/ijdb.072502sk> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-repro-package>,
