<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kondo & Asai (1995) Pomacanthus reaction-diffusion stripe insertion & Y-branch unzipping — Code-to-model traceability: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring (L22-66) now states Laws 4 and 5 with their Lean theorem names, the polar Laplacian, the threshold derivation, the fate/feedback bounds and the two new DOIs; each new function docstring names the paper figure or theorem it implements; the math-KG loop file registers both new laws with `lean_decl`, `lean_theorem`, `lean_locus` and `code_locus` (L76-116) and the Pass 2 code loci were corrected to the current line numbers. Deductions: the agent rule constants 0.9 / 0.1 / 0.35 / 0.3 (L846-848, L911-912) and the 0.004 fluctuation amplitude (L669) have no cited provenance in code or docstring (-4); panel titles were abbreviated to fit and no longer carry the full mechanism names (-1); the KG `lean_code` excerpts elide the proof bodies (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py L845–L848: Agent rule probabilities and softness are uncited defaults <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py#L845-L848>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kondo & Asai (1995) Pomacanthus reaction-diffusion stripe insertion & Y-branch unzipping — Model fidelity to source: 95/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Adds the two mechanisms the v2 audit asked for. The polar-sector Laplacian (`build_polar_sector_laplacian`, L606-646) carries the (1/rho) d/drho and (1/rho^2) d^2/dtheta^2 terms with mirrored-ghost Neumann edges and is unit-tested (annihilates constants, Lap(rho^2) = 4); `simulate_curvilinear_c_shaped_arc_insertion` (L659-819) rescales it by 1/R(t)^2 on the growing radius and refactors the sparse LU every 20 steps, recovering lambda_c to 1.06 % at s = 1 and the 3 -> 6 doubling with I_mid(s) strictly decreasing until insertion. The hybrid agent model (L837-961) implements the threshold fate rule, Nakamasu-style exclusion/support contacts and the bounded c_3/c_5 feedback that Lean Theorem 5 bounds. Deductions: the domain is an idealised sector (rho_in = 0.25, theta_half = 100 deg) rather than the specimen outline (-2); insertion needs injected 0.004 fluctuations (L733), and the older 1D kymograph still uses mode-6/12 biased nudges (L402-406) (-2); the agent rules are 1D and their probabilities are uncited heuristics (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py L402–L406: Pre-existing 1D kymograph injects mode-6 and mode-12 cosines every 25 steps to nucleate insertions (biased toward the expected answer) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py#L402-L406>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kondo & Asai (1995) Pomacanthus reaction-diffusion stripe insertion & Y-branch unzipping — Morphometric validation: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1204-1316) now returns 9 reference-anchored measurements: the four new ones are the curvilinear arc count after growth (6 vs reference 6, all five transects), I_mid at first insertion (0.742 vs the proved threshold 0.625, with the ~19 % discrepancy explained rather than hidden), the specimen radial arc spacing (2.62 mm vs the row-wise 3.80 mm of the same specimen) and the agent fate concordance (0.930 vs the ideal 1.0, with the full kappa ablation in the note). All carry units, methods and references. Deductions: the I_mid reference comparison fails at face value (ratio 1.19) because the effective threshold with diffusive activator supply is not derived (-3); the specimen arc count (8) is not placed in the model's cascade quantitatively beyond a remark (-2); final curved-domain spacing after insertion (1.33 lambda_c, CV 0.14) shows the cascade is not relaxed at s = 2.6, so wavelength homeostasis on the curved domain is asserted only at s = 1 (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py L1226–L1234: Final spacing 1.33 lambda_c (CV 0.14) at s = 2.6 shows an unrelaxed post-insertion cascade <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py#L1226-L1234>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-measurement-2d-p-imperator-y-junction-branch-point-horizontal-unzipping-displacement>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-measurement-curvilinear-c-shaped-polar-sector-kondo-asai-concentric-arc-count-after-radial-growth-s-1-2-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-measurement-discrete-iridophore-melanophore-agent-fate-concordance-with-the-kondo-asai-activator-partition-a-a>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-measurement-kondo-asai-1995-critical-diffusivity-ratio-d-c-d-i-d-a-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-measurement-mid-trough-inhibitor-i-mid-at-first-concentric-arc-insertion-vs-zero-activator-threshold-c-3-c-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-measurement-p-semicirculatus-specimen-concentric-arc-radial-spacing-curvature-corrected-inter-stripe-wavelength>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-measurement-p-semicirculatus-supercritical-d-i-0-10-vs-subcritical-control-d-i-0-05-stripe-count-delta>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-measurement-pomacanthus-semicirculatus-juvenile-specimen-inter-stripe-wavelength>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-measurement-simulated-1d-kondo-asai-piecewise-linear-pde-stripe-wavelength-vs-analytical-lambda-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kondo & Asai (1995) Pomacanthus reaction-diffusion stripe insertion & Y-branch unzipping — MorphoEval overall 93.1/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 remediation re-score of `1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py` (93.1/100, up from 92.0 in Pass 2). Both v2 remediation items are closed with mechanism, not presentation: a curvilinear C-shaped polar-sector Kondo-Asai solver with the (1/rho) d/drho curvature term and a growing outer radius reproduces 3 -> 6 concentric arc insertion (initial radial spacing = lambda_c +/- 1.06 %, angular coherence 1.000 -> 0.9996, insertion at s* = 2.18 when the monotonically falling mid-trough inhibitor reaches 0.742 vs the proved zero-activator threshold 0.625), anchored on the specimen by a structure-tensor concentric-centre fit (8 arcs, radial spacing 2.62 mm vs the oblique row-wise 3.80 mm); and a discrete 128-cell iridophore/melanophore agent lattice coupled to the fields through bounded feedback reproduces the 6-stripe partition (fate concordance 0.93-0.97, agent stripes = field stripes for all kappa, +3.6..+11.7 % contrast gain). Two new Lean 4 theorems (5 total, 0 sorrys) formalise the threshold partition and the fate/feedback bounds. The next layer of defects is structural: the sector geometry is not fitted to the specimen outline, the effective insertion threshold is ~19 % above the proved bound, the agent layer is 1D/periodic with heuristic rule probabilities, and arc insertion still relies on injected background fluctuations. Overall 93.1/100 (faithfulness 93.2, reproducibility 92.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 95, Morphological realism / specimen match 92, Parameter expressivity 93, Morphometric validation 93, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/pomacanthus_stripe_insertion_comparison.png: rendered output of 1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py at d58a084, image/png, 1309313 B, 2310×2044 px, artifact_sha256 92f926e73a7ebb81a69b893404cb09fadddfe38cba44064f55014e57a01e18c0 (sha256 92f926e73a7ebb81a69b893404cb09fadddfe38cba44064f55014e57a01e18c0), spec_fingerprint 9fca66f1ec5b7b985311e657c901c9004c5c9be93f2d029fa8365f8bf5322678. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 9fca66f1ec5b7b985311e657c901c9004c5c9be93f2d029fa8365f8bf5322678; artifact_sha256: 92f926e73a7ebb81a69b893404cb09fadddfe38cba44064f55014e57a01e18c0; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/pomacanthus_stripe_insertion/pomacanthus_semicirculatus_specimen.jpg=5564f850c1905fb6..., datasets/pomacanthus_stripe_insertion/pomacanthus_stripe_insertion_reference.json=915a886aac71c336..., datasets/pomacanthus_stripe_insertion/scout_manifest.json=bf877731da64b97b...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Kondo & Asai (1995) Nature 376(6543):765-768 piecewise-linear saturating Gierer-Meinhardt reaction-diffusion PDE on an expanding skin domain L(t) = L_0 exp(gamma t), mid-trough secondary stripe insertion cascade (3 -> 6 -> 12 -> 24 stripes) in Pomacanthus semicirculatus, and 2D horizontal Y-junction branch point unzipping in Pomacanthus imperator | Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) Kybernetik 12:30-39 short-range autocatalytic activation and long-range lateral inhibition | Nakamasu et al. (2009) PNAS 106:8429-8434 pigment-cell interaction network (short-range mutual exclusion, long-range support) and Bullara & De Decker (2015) lattice chromatophore model; reconstructed_in_script: 1D and 2D IMEX spectral solvers for the Kondo-Asai piecewise-linear saturating PDE across stationary domain doubling scales s in {1, 2, 4, 8} (body length 2, 4, 8, 16 cm -> 3, 6, 12, 24 stripes), subcritical inhibitor-diffusion control D_I = 0.050 < d_c D_A (0 stripes), continuous growing-domain kymograph (3 -> 6 -> 12 stripes), and 2D Y-branch horizontal unzipping (3 -> 4 stripes, +0.663 domain fraction displacement) | Pass 3: curvilinear C-shaped polar-sector solver (rho in [0.25, 1], theta in [-100, 100] deg, 48 x 96, sparse-LU IMEX) with growing outer radius; 3 -> 6 concentric arcs at s* = 2.18 with mid-trough inhibitor trace I_mid(s) against the zero-activator threshold c_3/|c_2| = 0.625; 1D hybrid field + 128-cell iridophore/melanophore agent lattice with contact rules and bounded feedback kappa on c_3/c_5, ablated over kappa in {0, 0.005, 0.01, 0.02} | Computer-vision segmentation of juvenile Pomacanthus semicirculatus specimen (`pomacanthus_semicirculatus_specimen.jpg`, CC BY-SA 4.0): 115 row-wise inter-stripe spacings (3.80 mm at 40 mm body span, CV = 0.34), primary/secondary prominence ratio 2.65x, bimodal Kondo-Asai waveform r = 0.858, and (Pass 3) structure-tensor concentric-arc fit (centre (262, 217) px, 8 arc radii, curvature-corrected radial spacing 2.62 mm, CV 0.28); transfer_boundary: The curvilinear domain is an idealised polar sector (fixed rho_in = 0.25, theta_half = 100 deg), not the specimen's body silhouette; its centre and radial extent are not fitted to the specimen's concentric centre, so arc angular spans are not compared | The agent layer is 1D on a periodic L = 6 lambda_c domain, so the wavelength is quantised to L/6 and only stripe contrast responds to the feedback; the rule probabilities (0.9 / 0.1 / update rate 0.35 / softness 0.3) are modelling choices, not values from Nakamasu et al. (2009) | The mid-trough threshold c_3/|c_2| = 0.625 is the A = 0 sufficient condition; the simulated insertion fires at I_mid = 0.742 because flanking arcs supply activator diffusively; does_not_claim: 2D agent-field coupling on the curved domain, pigment-cell migration or Delta-Notch-type contact signalling, a conformal map of the real body outline, or 3D body-fin boundary mechanics." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py:1236-1245 — insertion fires at I_mid = 0.742, 19 % above the proved A = 0 threshold 0.625; record A_trough at insertion and test the corrected local condition I < (c_3 + c_1 A_trough)/|c_2| plus the diffusive activator flux, and add a Lean theorem for the corrected threshold so the measurement matches its reference.",
        "remediation needed: 1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py:402-406 and 733 — both growing-domain solvers rely on injected fluctuations (mode-6/12 cosines in the 1D kymograph; 0.004 white noise on the curved domain) to nucleate insertion; add a nudge = 0 control and a nudge-amplitude sweep that reports the insertion scale s* as a function of fluctuation amplitude.",
        "remediation needed: 1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py:659-672 and 1106-1198 — the polar sector is an idealised rho_in = 0.25, theta_half = 100 deg domain; fit rho_in and theta_half from the specimen's concentric centre and arc radii (r_1/r_8 = 0.21, measured angular spans 31-358 deg) and compare the simulated per-arc angular spans with the measured `arc_angular_spans_deg` as a new measurement.",
        "remediation needed: 1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py:837-961 — the agent layer is 1D on a periodic domain (wavelength quantised to L/6) with uncited rule probabilities 0.9 / 0.1 / 0.35 / 0.3; port the fate lattice onto the curved 2D sector and calibrate the contact-rule rates to Nakamasu et al. (2009) ablation time scales so that the feedback can move spacing, not only contrast.",
        "remediation needed: 1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py:98-105 — pin the SHA-256 of `pomacanthus_stripe_insertion_reference.json` in `EXPECTED_SHA256` (or a versioned digest table) so edits to reference values fail the self-test, and extend the GIF (L1738-1811) with the curvilinear arc insertion so the animated artifact matches the Pass 3 figure." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.31e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kondo & Asai (1995) Pomacanthus reaction-diffusion stripe insertion & Y-branch unzipping — Parameter expressivity: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "In addition to the v2 sweeps (D_I dispersion family, 5 ontogenetic regimes, continuous growth), Pass 3 adds a continuous radial-growth axis s in [1, 2.6] on the curved domain with the arc count and I_mid recorded every 50 steps (L743-761), and a feedback-strength ablation `agent_coupling_ablation_sweep` over kappa in {0, 0.005, 0.01, 0.02} (L964-991) whose uncoupled kappa = 0 member is a genuine control; concordance, iridophore fraction and contrast gain all respond monotonically in the expected direction. Deductions: the sector shape parameters (rho_in, theta_half) and the agent rule probabilities are not swept, so their influence on arc curvature and concordance is unknown (-4); on the periodic agent domain the wavelength cannot respond to kappa (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py L659–L672: rho_in, theta_half_deg, nudge, s_final are exposed as arguments but only the defaults are exercised <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py#L659-L672>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kondo & Asai (1995) Pomacanthus reaction-diffusion stripe insertion & Y-branch unzipping — Reproducibility package: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`run_self_test` (L1817-1925) grows from 3 to 6 numbered blocks: the polar Laplacian is unit-tested, the curvilinear solver is checked for 3 -> 6 arcs on all transects, lambda_c recovery, coherence, insertion window, monotone I_mid and cache/bitwise determinism; the agent model is checked for 6 = 6 stripes, concordance >= 0.9, monotone contrast gain and seeded determinism; the specimen fit for arc count, spacing bounds and a plausible centre; and the 9 measurements for references. Runtime is 9.4 s (self-test) and 10.5 s (PNG + GIF), well under the 3-minute budget. Deductions: the two `pcolormesh` shading warnings on Panel G are not silenced (-2); the GIF was not extended to the curvilinear or agent mechanisms, so the animated artifact lags the figure (-3); the reference JSON is not SHA-pinned (see source-traceability) and the run writes a matplotlib cache unless MPLCONFIGDIR is set (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py L1738–L1811: GIF renderer unchanged from Pass 2: shows only the 1D planar insertion kymograph <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py#L1738-L1811>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-repro-package-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-repro-package-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kondo & Asai (1995) Pomacanthus reaction-diffusion stripe insertion & Y-branch unzipping — Source and data traceability: 94/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The vendored dataset gains the two new primary sources in `paper_citations.bib` (Nakamasu et al. 2009 `10.1073/pnas.0808622106`, Bullara & De Decker 2015 `10.1038/ncomms7971`), a `pass3_curvilinear_and_agent_coupling` block in the reference JSON recording the sector parameters, the insertion threshold derivation, the specimen body polygon, concentric centre, arc radii and the agent rule parameters, and a README section describing how each was derived; the SHA-256-pinned specimen and scout manifest are untouched and still verified at runtime (L111-129). Deductions: the reference JSON is hashed at runtime but not pinned in `EXPECTED_SHA256` (L98-105), so an edit to the reference values would not fail the self-test (-3); the Nakamasu rules are cited for their qualitative structure only (-2); the 40 mm body-span calibration still has no primary source (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
