<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Kondo & Asai (1995) Piecewise-Linear Saturating Activator-Inhibitor Steady State & Uniform Stability" ;
    dct:description "Proves that the interior equilibrium (A^*, I^*) = (3.0, 2.5) lies strictly inside the unsaturated linear window (0 < F^* = 0.09 < 0.20, 0 < G^* = 0.15 < 0.50) and is asymptotically stable to uniform perturbations (tr J = -0.01 < 0, det J = 0.005 > 0) | Variables: A, I: activator and inhibitor concentrations; c_1..c_5: linear synthesis coefficients; g_A, g_I: decay rates; F_max, G_max: upper saturation ceilings; (A^*, I^*) = (3.0, 2.5): interior homogeneous steady state" ;
    dct:source "Kondo & Asai (1995) Nature 376(6543):765-768 Fig. 1 legend; Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) Kybernetik 12(1):30-39" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py#L141-L225>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_004_pomacanthus_stripe_insertion.lean#L19-L54> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def clip_rate (S_max raw : Int) : Int := min S_max (max 0 raw)
def kondo_trace (f_A g_I_prime D_A D_I q : Int) : Int := (f_A + g_I_prime) - (D_A + D_I) * q
def kondo_det (f_A f_I g_A_prime g_I_prime D_A D_I q : Int) : Int :=
  (D_A * D_I) * (q * q) - (D_I * f_A + D_A * g_I_prime) * q + (f_A * g_I_prime - f_I * g_A_prime)
theorem kondo_asai_1995_piecewise_gm_steady_state_and_uniform_stability (D_A D_I : Int) :
    clip_rate 200 (80 * 3 + (-80) * 5 / 2 + 50) = 90 ∧
    clip_rate 500 (100 * 3 - 150) = 150 ∧
    kondo_trace 50 (-60) D_A D_I 0 = -10 ∧
    kondo_det 50 (-80) 100 (-60) D_A D_I 0 = 5000 := by
  unfold clip_rate kondo_trace kondo_det; refine ⟨by decide, by decide, by omega, by omega⟩
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "F(A^*, I^*) = min(F_max, max(0, c_1 A^* + c_2 I^* + c_3)) = g_A A^*,  G(A^*, I^*) = min(G_max, max(0, c_4 A^* + c_5)) = g_I I^*;  tr J = f_A + g'_I < 0 ∧ det J = f_A g'_I - f_I g'_A > 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/376765a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms7971>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0808622106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1387/ijdb.072502sk> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Growing-Domain Reaction-Diffusion" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_004.kondo_det" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_004.kondo_asai_1995_piecewise_gm_steady_state_and_uniform_stability" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Kondo & Asai (1995) Turing Wave Instability Threshold (D_I / D_A > d_c)" ;
    dct:description "Proves that the canonical Kondo-Asai diffusivity ratio d = 100/7 ≈ 14.29 exceeds d_c ≈ 10.26 and drives det M(q) = -2440 < 0 at q = 3, whereas subcritical inhibitor diffusion (D_I = 0.050, d = 7.14 < d_c) keeps det M(q) > 0 | Variables: D_A = 0.007, D_I = 0.10: activator and inhibitor diffusivities; d = D_I / D_A = 14.29: diffusivity ratio; d_c = 10.26: critical Turing ratio; k_c^2 = 3.2714: critical squared wavenumber; λ_c = 2π / k_c = 3.4739: intrinsic stripe wavelength" ;
    dct:source "Kondo & Asai (1995) Nature 376(6543):765-768 Fig. 1" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py#L153-L250>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_004_pomacanthus_stripe_insertion.lean#L61-L78> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """theorem kondo_asai_1995_turing_wave_instability_and_subcritical_stability :
    kondo_det 50 (-80) 100 (-60) 7 100 3 = -2440 ∧
    kondo_det 50 (-80) 100 (-60) 7 50 3 = 1910 ∧
    kondo_det 50 (-80) 100 (-60) 7 7 3 = 5651 := by
  decide
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "d = D_I / D_A > d_c = 5.2 + 1.6√10 ≈ 10.26 ⟹ det M(k_c^2) < 0 at k_c^2 = (D_I f_A + D_A g'_I) / (2 D_A D_I) = 229 / 70" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/376765a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms7971>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0808622106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1387/ijdb.072502sk> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Growing-Domain Reaction-Diffusion" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_004.kondo_det" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_004.kondo_asai_1995_turing_wave_instability_and_subcritical_stability" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Kondo & Asai (1995) P. semicirculatus Mid-Trough Doubling Cascade vs P. imperator Y-Branch Unzipping" ;
    dct:description "Formalizes the species-specific wavelength-homeostasis laws in Pomacanthus: simultaneous 1D mid-trough secondary stripe insertion (3 → 6 → 12 → 24) in P. semicirculatus versus 2D horizontal Y-branch dislocation unzipping (+1 stripe per branch) in P. imperator | Variables: s = L(t)/L_0: ontogenetic body-length doubling scale (2 → 4 → 8 → 16 cm); N_0 = 3: initial juvenile stripe count; u: number of horizontally unzipped 2D Y-junction branch points" ;
    dct:source "Kondo & Asai (1995) Nature 376(6543):765-768 Figs. 1-4; Crampin, Gaffney & Maini (1999) Bull. Math. Biol. 61(6):1093-1120" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py#L256-L480>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_004_pomacanthus_stripe_insertion.lean#L85-L114> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def semicirculatus_stripes (N_0 s : Nat) : Nat := N_0 * s
def imperator_unzipped_stripes (N_0 unzipped_branches : Nat) : Nat := N_0 + unzipped_branches
theorem kondo_asai_1995_semicirculatus_insertion_vs_imperator_unzipping :
    semicirculatus_stripes 3 1 = 3 ∧
    semicirculatus_stripes 3 2 = 6 ∧
    semicirculatus_stripes 3 4 = 12 ∧
    semicirculatus_stripes 3 8 = 24 ∧
    imperator_unzipped_stripes 3 1 = 4 := by
  unfold semicirculatus_stripes imperator_unzipped_stripes; omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "L(t) = s L_0 (s ∈ {1,2,4,8}) ⟹ N_semicirculatus(s) = 3 s ∈ {3,6,12,24} (λ(s) = λ_c);  N_imperator(N_0, u) = N_0 + u" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/376765a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms7971>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0808622106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1387/ijdb.072502sk> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Growing-Domain Reaction-Diffusion" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_004.semicirculatus_stripes" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_004.kondo_asai_1995_semicirculatus_insertion_vs_imperator_unzipping" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Kondo & Asai (1995) Curvilinear C-Shaped Mid-Trough Inhibitor Threshold Partition for Concentric Arc Insertion (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Proves the threshold partition that drives de novo concentric arc insertion in the curvilinear solver: in an activator-depleted trough the piecewise-linear synthesis is silent for I ≥ 0.625 and active below it (antitone in I), so arcs insert exactly when the inhibitor minimum between stretched arcs crosses the threshold; concentric arc number doubles with radial span while arc length grows strictly with arc index (the polar (1/ρ)∂_ρ term shifts phase, not count) | Variables: ρ = r/R(t): scaled radius on the posterior-centred C-shaped sector; θ: polar angle; s = R(t)/R_0: radial growth scale; I_mid: mid-trough inhibitor minimum along the central radial transect; I_thr = c_3/|c_2| = 0.625: zero-activator insertion threshold (625 in 10^3-scaled Int units); N_0 = 3: equilibrated concentric arcs" ;
    dct:source "Kondo & Asai (1995) Nature 376(6543):765-768 Fig. 1d-f; Crampin, Gaffney & Maini (1999) Bull. Math. Biol. 61(6):1093-1120" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py#L592-L819>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_004_pomacanthus_stripe_insertion.lean#L114-L176> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def trough_synthesis (I : Int) : Int := clip_rate 200 ((-80) * I / 1000 + 50)
def concentric_arcs (N_0 s : Nat) : Nat := N_0 * s
def arc_length_pi (R_in lam k : Nat) : Nat := R_in + lam * k
theorem kondo_asai_1995_curvilinear_mid_trough_threshold_partition :
    trough_synthesis 2500 = 0 ∧ trough_synthesis 625 = 0 ∧
    trough_synthesis 600 = 2 ∧ trough_synthesis 0 = 50 ∧
    (∀ I : Int, 625 ≤ I → trough_synthesis I = 0) ∧
    (∀ I₁ I₂ : Int, I₁ ≤ I₂ → trough_synthesis I₂ ≤ trough_synthesis I₁) ∧
    concentric_arcs 3 2 = 6 ∧
    (∀ R_in lam k : Nat, 0 < lam → arc_length_pi R_in lam k < arc_length_pi R_in lam (k + 1)) := by
  refine ⟨by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, ?_, ?_, by decide, ?_⟩ <;> ...  -- omega / Nat.add_lt_add_left
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Lap_phys = R^-2 [∂²_ρ + ρ^-1 ∂_ρ + ρ^-2 ∂²_θ] on ρ ∈ [ρ_in, 1], θ ∈ [-Θ, Θ], R(t) = R_0 s(t);  F_trough(I) = min(F_max, max(0, c_2 I + c_3)) = 0 ⟺ I ≥ I_thr = c_3/|c_2| = 0.625;  I_1 ≤ I_2 ⟹ F_trough(I_2) ≤ F_trough(I_1);  N_arcs(s) = N_0 s (3 → 6);  π(R_in + kλ) < π(R_in + (k+1)λ)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/376765a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms7971>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0808622106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1387/ijdb.072502sk> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Growing-Domain Reaction-Diffusion" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_004.trough_synthesis" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_004.kondo_asai_1995_curvilinear_mid_trough_threshold_partition" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Discrete Iridophore/Melanophore Agent Fate Partition Coupled to the Kondo-Asai Activator Field with Bounded Feedback (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Formalizes the hybrid continuum-agent coupling: the deterministic fate partition is monotone and binary (so iridophores occupy activator peaks and melanophores the troughs), and the agent feedback perturbs the Kondo-Asai source terms within bounded intervals, preserving the Jacobian sign structure; the stochastic contact rules (short-range exclusion, long-range support) in the script are abstracted from Nakamasu et al. (2009) | Variables: A: local macroscopic activator read by a discrete pigment cell; A_thr = A^* = 3.0 (3000 in 10^3-scaled Int units): fate threshold; fate = 1 iridophore/light-stripe cell, 0 melanophore/dark-interstripe cell; κ_A, κ_I: agent-to-field feedback strengths added to the basal synthesis rates c_3, c_5" ;
    dct:source "Nakamasu, Takahashi, Kanbe & Kondo (2009) PNAS 106(21):8429-8434; Bullara & De Decker (2015) Nat. Commun. 6:6971; Kondo & Asai (1995) Nature 376(6543):765-768" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py#L821-L991>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_004_pomacanthus_stripe_insertion.lean#L179-L229> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def cell_fate (A A_thr : Int) : Int := if A_thr ≤ A then 1 else 0
def coupled_c3 (c3 kappa_A fate : Int) : Int := c3 + kappa_A * fate
def coupled_c5 (c5 kappa_I fate : Int) : Int := c5 + kappa_I * (1 - fate)
theorem kondo_asai_1995_pigment_agent_fate_partition_and_bounded_feedback :
    (∀ A₁ A₂ A_thr : Int, A₁ ≤ A₂ → cell_fate A₁ A_thr ≤ cell_fate A₂ A_thr) ∧
    (∀ A A_thr : Int, cell_fate A A_thr = 0 ∨ cell_fate A A_thr = 1) ∧
    cell_fate 3000 3000 = 1 ∧ cell_fate 0 3000 = 0 ∧
    (∀ c3 kappa_A A A_thr : Int, 0 ≤ kappa_A → c3 ≤ coupled_c3 c3 kappa_A (cell_fate A A_thr) ∧ coupled_c3 c3 kappa_A (cell_fate A A_thr) ≤ c3 + kappa_A) ∧
    (∀ c5 kappa_I A A_thr : Int, 0 ≤ kappa_I → c5 ≤ coupled_c5 c5 kappa_I (cell_fate A A_thr) ∧ coupled_c5 c5 kappa_I (cell_fate A A_thr) ≤ c5 + kappa_I) := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, by decide, by decide, ?_, ?_⟩ <;> ...  -- split <;> omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "fate(A) = [A ≥ A_thr] ∈ {0, 1}, A_1 ≤ A_2 ⟹ fate(A_1) ≤ fate(A_2);  c_3 ↦ c_3 + κ_A fate ∈ [c_3, c_3 + κ_A];  c_5 ↦ c_5 + κ_I (1 - fate) ∈ [c_5, c_5 + κ_I]  (κ_A, κ_I ≥ 0)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/376765a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms7971>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0808622106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1387/ijdb.072502sk> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Growing-Domain Reaction-Diffusion" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_004.cell_fate" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_004.kondo_asai_1995_pigment_agent_fate_partition_and_bounded_feedback" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

